-- title:
--   Centredness of a Drinfeld chart isomorphism intertwining automorphisms
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and, for two complete discrete valuation rings: let $W_0$ be a domain that is a discrete valuation ring, adically complete for its maximal ideal, let $t_0 \in W_0$ and let $f_0, u_0, v_0 \in W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $f_0 - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1)$ lying in $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$; let $W$ be likewise a domain, discrete valuation ring, adically complete, let $t \in W$ lie in the maximal ideal of $W$, and let $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$. Put $S_0 = W_0[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(t_0)v_0 - f_0u_0)$ and $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(t)v - fu)$, and let $J_0 \subseteq S_0$, $J \subseteq S$ be the ideals generated by the images of $X_0, X_1$. Assume given a ring isomorphism $\beta : S_0 \simeq S$ and a ring isomorphism $\beta_W : W_0 \simeq W$ with $\beta(C(w)) = C(\beta_W(w))$ in $S$ for all $w \in W_0$; ring automorphisms $\theta_0$ of $S_0$ and $\theta$ of $S$ with $\beta \circ \theta_0 = \theta \circ \beta$ pointwise, with $\theta$ fixing the image of $C(w)$ for every $w \in W$ and with $\theta(X_j) \in J$ for $j = 0,1$; and a matrix $M_0 \in M_2(W_0)$ such that $\theta_0(X_j) - \sum_i C((M_0)_{ij})X_i \in J_0^2$ for $j = 0,1$, with $\det(1 - M_0)$ a unit in $W_0$. The conclusion is that $\beta(X_j) \in J$ for $j = 0,1$, i.e. $\beta(J_0) \subseteq J$.
--
--   This is the centring step for isomorphisms of Drinfeld charts of a completed supersingular stalk, in the style of Katz–Mazur's local analysis: an isomorphism between two such charts that intertwines a pair of automorphisms whose linear part $M_0$ has $\det(1-M_0)$ invertible must carry the chart's maximal-point ideal into the corresponding one, so that it is centred at the distinguished point. It is used in the transport of semilinear automorphism data between two charts, in [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_semilinear_linearPart_transport_of_forall_specialLinearGroup_of_dense`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_semilinear_linearPart_transport_of_forall_specialLinearGroup_of_dense) and its prime variant.
